\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Class breakdown of the 8,474,531-galaxy catalog. The three-class output is dominated by the \textsc  {not\_spiral}{} class (60.8\%), which captures ellipticals, irregulars, edge-on disks, and artifacts. Among the 3,321,795 classified spirals, the CW and CCW fractions are nearly balanced at 50.8\% and 49.2\% (raw) or 49.74\% and 50.26\% (equivariant), consistent with exact parity. }}{7}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:class_pie}{{5}{7}{Class breakdown of the 8,474,531-galaxy catalog. The three-class output is dominated by the \NS {} class (60.8\%), which captures ellipticals, irregulars, edge-on disks, and artifacts. Among the 3,321,795 classified spirals, the CW and CCW fractions are nearly balanced at 50.8\% and 49.2\% (raw) or 49.74\% and 50.26\% (equivariant), consistent with exact parity}{figure.5}{}}
